**Description**
---------------

**Build the Future with Us**

Are you driven by analyzing business needs and implementing technology solutions? Would you like to contribute to the purpose of a company that strives to help its clients feel confident and secure about their future?




As an IT Analyst, you will play a key role in supporting business partners, analyzing their needs, and delivering and evolving technology solutions for corporate sectors. You will also contribute to compliance activities, IT asset monitoring, and the execution of initiatives under your responsibility.




You will collaborate with business partners and IT teams to clarify needs, assess impacts, document requirements, and ensure that delivered solutions meet expectations.




This position is an excellent opportunity to showcase your skills and fully leverage your potential within a caring and trustworthy organization. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.




**What You Will Accomplish With Us**
------------------------------------

As an IT Analyst, you will be at the core of our mission. Your main responsibilities will include:




* Support business partners in clarifying, prioritizing, and validating their needs, facilitate analysis workshops, and document processes, business rules, and functional requirements;
* Assess the business, functional, operational, and technological impacts of proposed changes, and translate needs into clear requirements for design and delivery teams;
* Develop analyses, recommendations, and solution options to support decision-making;
* Collaborate with project managers, designers, architects, and other contributors in delivering initiatives;
* Define and coordinate functional validation activities and user acceptance testing, support users throughout testing, and follow up on defects and corrective actions;
* Maintain clear, structured, and up-to-date functional documentation;
* Coordinate the follow-up of commitments, action plans, audits, and compliance requirements related to your files, and contribute to the monitoring of IT recovery plans, business continuity exercises, and resulting actions;
* Support the evolution of IT assets, including risks, obsolescence, controls, and roadmaps, and prepare the follow-ups, analyses, and indicators required to report on progress and issues;




**What Could Accelerate Your Success in This Role**
---------------------------------------------------

We are looking for someone who:




* Is recognized for their autonomy, rigor, organizational skills, and proactive approach, developed through significant experience in IT analysis or business analysis;
* Stands out through excellent analytical, synthesis, writing, and communication skills, as well as experience in requirements analysis, documentation, and functional validation;
* Demonstrates a strong ability to coordinate multiple initiatives simultaneously and influence stakeholders without direct authority, while contributing to initiatives related to IT processes, risk management, and compliance requirements;
* Has a solid understanding of IT processes and business environments, supported by education in information technology, administration, business analysis, or a related field;
* Has knowledge of the insurance and financial services industry, which is considered an asset;
* Has experience related to IT asset management, IT disaster recovery plans, obsolescence management, or portfolio management, which is considered an asset;
* Has knowledge of Excel, Power BI, or similar tools to produce analyses and monitoring reports, which is considered an asset;
* Has an advanced level of French and an intermediate level of English, as the individual will communicate with unilingual English-speaking partners across Canada through emails and phone calls on a weekly basis;




**Why You Will Love Working With Us**
-------------------------------------

* A work environment where learning and development blend with a collective pursuit of excellence;
* Artificial intelligence is available to everyone, increasing personal efficiency and supporting organizational growth;
* A healthy, safe, equitable, and inclusive work environment where potential can flourish and develop freely;
* The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment, supported by flexibility and access to inspiring and innovative workspaces;




**Competitive Benefits**
------------------------

* Flexible group insurance plans;
* Competitive retirement savings plan;
* Employee share purchase plan;
* Vacation program and wellness/personal development days;
* Telemedicine;
* Employee and Family Assistance Program;
* Ergonomic furniture program;
* Performance bonus;
* Discounts on iA products;
* And much more!




**Apply Now and Take the Lead in Your Career**
----------------------------------------------

Join us where your talent truly matters!




**Not Sure Whether to Apply?**
------------------------------

At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, take a chance and apply. Your place may be with us, and we would love to get to know you!

**Get ahead of your career, where your talent belongs**
-------------------------------------------------------

See why so many people choose iA!

**Company Overview**
--------------------

iA Financial Group is the strength of a company with a human side, with its over 10,000 employees. Together, we have earned the trust of our more than five million clients and 50,000 advisors who have chosen us for their insurance, savin

**Why should you join our team?**

Innergex Renewable Energy Inc. is an independent renewable energy producer with an extensive and growing portfolio of assets in Canada, the United States, France and Chile. The Corporation develops, acquires, owns and operates hydroelectric facilities, wind farms, solar farms and energy storage facilities.

For more than 30 years, Innergex has believed in a world where abundant renewable energy promotes healthier communities and creates shared prosperity. We are convinced that generating power from renewable sources will lead the way to a better world. We remain committed to responsible growth that balances people, our planet, and prosperity. We believe in offering an engaging, inclusive and supportive work environment where each team member can thrive.

**Your contribution!**

Reporting to the Senior Manager - IT Infrastructure, the Systems Administrator plays a key role in the operation, evolution, and security of the company’s technology environments. Working alongside a team of specialists, the person ensures the smooth operation of hybrid infrastructures (on-premises and cloud-based) that support Innergex’s corporate operations and renewable energy facilities in Canada, the United States, France, and Chile. They participate in large-scale technology projects, the optimization of IT and OT environments, process automation, and the maintenance of high standards of performance, availability, and cybersecurity. The person in this role will be required to participate in a rotating on-call schedule to ensure support for critical infrastructure outside of normal working hours, including evenings and weekends.

**Your day-to day!**

* Administer and evolve Windows, Azure, Microsoft 365, and VMware environments.
* Ensure the operation of hybrid infrastructures (on-premises and cloud-based) and data centers.
* Manage essential services such as Active Directory, Entra ID, Exchange, VDI, virtual servers, and SaaS/PaaS solutions.
* Analyze system performance, capacity, and security to ensure stability and availability.
* Participate in the implementation of new technological solutions and the continuous improvement of infrastructure.
* Help resolve complex incidents and serve as a technical expert for internal teams.
* Monitor IT environments and respond to security and operational alerts.
* Collaborate with operations and construction teams to support renewable energy production sites.
* Automate certain administrative tasks using scripts and appropriate tools.
* Participate in system updates, scheduled maintenance, and optimization.
* Participate in a rotating on-call schedule and contribute to operational continuity by providing support for critical infrastructure when required.
* Maintain thorough and up-to-date technical documentation.
* Contribute to audits, IT controls, and adherence to compliance and cybersecurity requirements.
* Serve as an advisor to the team on best practices and emerging technologies.

**Your skills, our requirements!**

* Bilingualism (French and English, both spoken and written) is required to collaborate with various stakeholders outside Quebec on a regular basis.
* A minimum of 3 years of experience in systems administration
* Must be available and able to participate in a rotating on-call schedule and contribute to business continuity by providing support for critical infrastructure when required.

**Additional considerations!**

* The position is based at the company’s headquarters in Longueuil, steps away from the Longueuil-Université de Sherbrooke metro station.
* This position is at the P2 level.
* Competitive salary and annual bonus;
* Three weeks vacation to start and paid vacations during the holiday season;
* 100% Innergex-funded medical insurance from day one of employment, including primary care services through dialogue (or telemedicine) for permanent positions;
* Group retirement plans with employer participation;
* 100% Employer-funded Wellness Account;
* Electric vehicle (E-VIP) incentive program;
* Hybrid work model;
* Career development opportunities;
